.TH BOSWAS-PRESET 1 "November 2026" "boswas-branding 3.0~alpha1" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-preset \- list and switch the Boswas OS desktop presets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B current
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B apply
.I PRESET
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B reset
.SH DESCRIPTION
Boswas OS ships ten presets of one design system: Horizon, Midnight,
Aurora, Slate, Carbon, Pearl, Ocean, Ember, Nebula and Classic. Each is
light or dark and brings a wallpaper and a colour scheme for KDE
applications.
.PP
Applying a preset sets light or dark for the Boswas desktop
.RB ( boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-shell (1)):
the shell, the window frames and the lock screen; the wallpaper; and, for
KDE applications that are installed, their colours. The accent colour of
the shell, the icon theme, the panel and the background of the lock and
login screens do not change. A user who has not applied a preset has the
Boswas Prism look, which is not one of the ten.
.PP
The command writes the files named below itself and starts no other
program. Boswas Control Center (Personalization) uses it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
The presets with their identifier, name, description, light or dark variant
and accent colour, and the current preset.
.TP
.B current
The preset that was applied last. Nothing is printed when no preset has
been applied, or after
.BR reset .
.TP
.BI apply " PRESET"
Apply a preset for the signed-in user: write
.IR ~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml ,
merge the preset's colours into
.IR ~/.config/kdeglobals ,
record the choice in
.I ~/.config/boswasrc
and ask the running compositor to reload its configuration (without one,
the look applies at the next login). Runs as the desktop user; refused for
root.
.TP
.B reset
Return to the default look, Boswas Prism, which is no preset: remove
.IR ~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml ,
merge the Boswas Prism colours into
.IR ~/.config/kdeglobals ,
clear the recorded preset and ask the running compositor to reload. Runs as
the desktop user; refused for root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output:
.B list
prints the presets and the current one,
.B current
prints {"current": ...},
.B apply
prints {"applied": "\fIPRESET\fR"},
.B reset
prints {"reset": true, "default": "Boswas Prism"}, and an error prints its
message, the exit status and the step that failed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 a step failed (the message names it:
.BR appearance ,
.B colours
or
.BR record ),
2 unknown preset, 3 usage error, 4 run as root.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config
stands for
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when that is an absolute path. The new content of the three user files is
prepared before the first one is written. Each is replaced atomically (a new
file with mode 0600, then a rename). A file that is a symbolic link or not
a regular file is refused, and so is a symbolic link in the place of
.IR ~/.config/boswas :
the command then fails and changes nothing.
.TP
.I /usr/share/boswas/presets/presets.json
The preset definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml
Light or dark and the wallpaper, read by
.BR boswas-compositor (1).
Rewritten as a whole by every
.BR apply ,
removed by
.BR reset .
.TP
.I ~/.config/kdeglobals
The colours of KDE applications. Only the colour groups and the
ColorScheme entry are replaced.
.TP
.I ~/.config/boswasrc
The recorded choice ([Preset] Current). Other groups and keys are kept.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-control-center (1)
